# Web UI

`lib/web/` is Flutter Web UI. Layout and gotchas: `apps/reader_flutter/lib/web/CLAUDE.md`.

## Rules

- Gate web UI with `useWebShell(context)` in `lib/web/layout/app_layout_scope.dart`: `kIsWeb` and width ≥ 720 (`WebTokens.compactBreakpoint`).
- Below 720px the app renders `lib/mobile/`. A web-only feature also needs a mobile implementation or it disappears on a narrow browser.
- Read tier from `AppLayoutScope.tierOf(context)` (compact &lt; 720, medium 720–1099, expanded ≥ 1100). Wrap a new tier-aware body in `AppLayoutScopeBuilder` at the route adapter.
- Screen bodies are content only (`HomeScreenBody` and siblings). Chrome is `WebPageScaffold` or `WebShellScaffold`.
- Hover, multi-column grids, and `WebSidebar` stay in this folder.
- Import providers, models, and l10n from root `lib/`. Leave `lib/mobile/` and `lib/desktop/` unimported.
- Style with `WebTokens` and `AppColors`.

```dart
if (useWebShell(context)) {
  return const WebPageScaffold(body: HomeScreenBody());
}
```

Run: `make reader-run-web`. A release web build bakes `API_BASE_URL`; a host change needs a rebuild.
